        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I don't fully understand the problem, but the first idea that comes to mind is storing `H._error` from `xpcall` and then re-throwing it inside `picker_stop`, since you have to press a key anyway to close the picker. I also found that `api.nvim_echo` works, but only without the `err` flag. So perhaps this should be fixed in Neovim itself (lock state interrupt).\n\nThank you for taking a look at the problem. Anyway, I'll wait for your decision regarding the issue 🙂",
